<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>TRANCE — {{ findings.case.name }}</title>
<style>
  :root {
    --bg: #eef1f0; --surface: #ffffff; --surface-2: #e3e7e6; --ink: #1b2226; --ink-muted: #5b6570;
    --border: #c7cdcc; --accent: #a23e2a; --accent-bg: #f3e1dc; --confirm: #2f7a5c; --confirm-bg: #e1efe8;
    --noise: #92702c; --noise-bg: #efe9d8; --mono-chip-bg: #e7ebea;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(20, 24, 27, 0.06), 0 6px 20px rgba(20, 24, 27, 0.05);
  }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    :root:not([data-theme="light"]) {
      --bg: #14181b; --surface: #1b2126; --surface-2: #232a2f; --ink: #dce2e6; --ink-muted: #8b969c;
      --border: #313a40; --accent: #e2694f; --accent-bg: #33211c; --confirm: #4fae84; --confirm-bg: #1e2e27;
      --noise: #c9a552; --noise-bg: #2c2818; --mono-chip-bg: #232a2f;
      --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
    }
  }
  :root[data-theme="dark"] {
    --bg: #14181b; --surface: #1b2126; --surface-2: #232a2f; --ink: #dce2e6; --ink-muted: #8b969c;
    --border: #313a40; --accent: #e2694f; --accent-bg: #33211c; --confirm: #4fae84; --confirm-bg: #1e2e27;
    --noise: #c9a552; --noise-bg: #2c2818; --mono-chip-bg: #232a2f;
    --shadow: 0 1px 2px rgba(0,0,0,.3), 0 8px 24px rgba(0,0,0,.35);
  }
  * { box-sizing: border-box; }
  body { background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); margin: 0; font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, "Helvetica Neue", Arial, sans-serif; line-height: 1.55; }
  .page { max-width: 800px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 40px 24px 80px; }
  h1, h2, h3 { font-family: Georgia, "Iowan Old Style", "Times New Roman", serif; text-wrap: balance; margin: 0; color: var(--ink); }
  .eyebrow { font-family: ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", Consolas, monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  code, .mono { font-family: ui-monospace, "Cascadia Code", Consolas, "Liberation Mono", monospace; }
  .masthead { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 18px; padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--ink); margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .masthead-top { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 16px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .masthead h1 { font-size: 30px; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 6px; }
  .stamp { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent); border: 1.5px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 3px; padding: 7px 10px; transform: rotate(-2deg); white-space: nowrap; flex-shrink: 0; }
  .meta-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 130px 1fr; gap: 6px 14px; font-size: 13px; }
  .meta-grid dt { color: var(--ink-muted); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 11px; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; padding-top: 2px; }
  .meta-grid dd { margin: 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .flag-warn { color: var(--noise); font-weight: 600; }
  .flag-ok { color: var(--confirm); font-weight: 600; }
  section { margin-bottom: 44px; }
  .band { border-top: 2px solid var(--ink); padding-top: 22px; margin-top: 52px; }
  .band .eyebrow { margin-bottom: 4px; }
  .band h2 { font-size: 24px; font-weight: 600; margin-bottom: 20px; }
  .section-head { display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 16px; }
  .section-head h2 { font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; }
  .section-head .count { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  p { margin: 0 0 12px; color: var(--ink); max-width: 66ch; }
  .note { font-size: 13.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 62ch; }
  .tiles { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr); gap: 12px; }
  .tiles.three { grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); }
  @media (max-width: 560px) { .tiles, .tiles.three { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
  .tile { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 4px solid var(--confirm); border-radius: 6px; padding: 16px 18px; box-shadow: var(--shadow); }
  .tile.gap { border-left-color: var(--noise); }
  .tile.err { border-left-color: var(--accent); }
  .tile h3 { font-size: 15px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
  .tile p { font-size: 13px; color: var(--ink-muted); margin-bottom: 0; }
  .tile .tile-value { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12px; color: var(--ink); background: var(--mono-chip-bg); border-radius: 4px; padding: 4px 7px; display: inline-block; margin-top: 6px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .evidence-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden; box-shadow: var(--shadow); font-size: 13px; }
  .evidence-table th { text-align: left; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 10.5px; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); background: var(--surface-2); }
  .evidence-table td { padding: 10px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); vertical-align: top; }
  .evidence-table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }
  .evidence-table .val { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12px; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .evidence-table .off { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 11.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); white-space: nowrap; }
  .table-scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  .chip { display: inline-block; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 999px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .chip.high, .chip.ok { background: var(--confirm-bg); color: var(--confirm); }
  .chip.low, .chip.skipped, .chip.not_implemented { background: var(--noise-bg); color: var(--noise); }
  .chip.error { background: var(--accent-bg); color: var(--accent); }
  .path-list { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  .path-pill { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 5px; padding: 5px 10px; }
  .path-pill.odd { border-color: var(--noise); color: var(--noise); }
  .ribbon { background: var(--noise-bg); color: var(--noise); border: 1px solid var(--noise); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 16px; font-size: 13px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
  .ribbon strong { color: var(--noise); }
  .sequence { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; counter-reset: seq; }
  .sequence li { counter-increment: seq; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 30px 1fr; gap: 4px 12px; padding: 9px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); font-size: 13.5px; align-items: baseline; }
  .sequence li::before { content: counter(seq); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-muted); text-align: right; }
  .sequence li:last-child { border-bottom: none; }
  .seq-off { grid-column: 2; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 10.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  .seq-type { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 9.5px; letter-spacing: .05em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-muted); margin-right: 6px; }
  .seq-flag { font-size: 10px; color: var(--accent); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; margin-left: 6px; }
  .callout { background: var(--surface-2); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); border-radius: 0 5px 5px 0; padding: 10px 14px; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); margin: 10px 0 14px; }
  .callout strong { color: var(--ink); }
  details.appendix { background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 4px 16px; }
  details.appendix summary { cursor: pointer; padding: 12px 0; font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 12.5px; color: var(--ink-muted); }
  details.appendix summary:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 2px; }
  .appendix-body { padding-bottom: 14px; }
  .appendix-row { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 12px; font-size: 12px; padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }
  .appendix-row .val { font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; color: var(--ink-muted); overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .appendix-row .why { color: var(--ink-muted); text-align: right; flex-shrink: 0; max-width: 40%; }
  .reco-list { list-style: none; padding: 0; margin: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; }
  .reco-list li { position: relative; font-size: 13.5px; background: var(--surface); border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 6px; padding: 12px 14px 12px 44px; }
  .reco-list li::before { content: "→"; position: absolute; left: 14px; top: 12px; color: var(--accent); font-weight: 600; }
  footer { margin-top: 56px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); font-family: ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 11px; color: var(--ink-muted); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 8px; }
  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { animation: none !important; transition: none !important; } }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">

  {% set modules = findings.modules %}
  {% set ok_count = modules.values()|selectattr("status", "equalto", "ok")|list|length %}

  <div class="masthead">
    <div class="masthead-top">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">TRANCE · Forensic Artifact Triage · Case Report</div>
        <h1>{{ findings.case.name }}</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="stamp">Authorized security exercise<br>Test environment</div>
    </div>
    <dl class="meta-grid">
      <dt>Generated</dt><dd>{{ findings.generated_at }}</dd>
      <dt>Modules</dt><dd>{{ ok_count }} of {{ modules|length }} ran cleanly</dd>
      <dt>Artifacts</dt><dd>{{ findings.artifacts|length }} across all modules</dd>
      <dt>Output dir</dt><dd>{{ findings.case.output_dir }}</dd>
      {% if findings.case.evidence_dir %}<dt>Evidence dir</dt><dd>{{ findings.case.evidence_dir }}</dd>{% endif %}
    </dl>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Module status</h2></div>
    <div class="tiles three">
      {% for name, m in modules.items() %}
      <div class="tile{{ ' err' if m.status == 'error' else (' gap' if m.status != 'ok' else '') }}">
        <h3 class="mono" style="font-size:13px;">{{ name }}</h3>
        <p><span class="chip {{ m.status }}">{{ m.status.replace('_', ' ') }}</span>
        {% if m.status == 'ok' %} · {{ m.artifact_count }} artifact{{ 's' if m.artifact_count != 1 }}{% endif %}</p>
        {% if m.message %}<p style="margin-top:6px;">{{ m.message }}</p>{% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if registry %}
  <div class="band">
    <div class="eyebrow">Module A</div>
    <h2>Registry &amp; execution evidence</h2>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
      <dt>Hives analyzed</dt><dd>{{ registry.hives_analyzed|join(", ") if registry.hives_analyzed else "— none" }}</dd>
      {% if registry.hives_missing %}
      <dt>Hives not provided</dt><dd>{{ registry.hives_missing|join(", ") }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Summary</dt><dd>{{ registry.summary }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  {% if registry.errors %}
  <section>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Extraction errors:</strong> the findings below are from whichever hives/plugins succeeded; these did not.
      <ul style="margin:8px 0 0; padding-left:18px;">
        {% for err in registry.errors %}
        <li class="mono" style="font-size:12px;">{{ err }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Confirmed Tor Browser components</h2>
      <span class="count">{{ registry.component_timeline|length }} distinct file{{ "s" if registry.component_timeline|length != 1 }} — {{ registry.corroborated_components }} corroborated by 2+ independent hive sources</span>
    </div>
    {% if registry.component_timeline %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Seen in</th><th>Amcache first-seen</th><th>UserAssist runs</th><th>UserAssist last run</th><th>ShimCache hits</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in registry.component_timeline %}
          <tr>
            <td class="val">{{ c.basename }}{% if c.paths|length > 1 %}<br><span class="off">({{ c.paths|length }} path variants)</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="val">{% for t in c.seen_in %}<span class="chip {{ 'high' if t in ('UserAssist', 'Amcache') else 'low' if t == 'RecentDocs' else '' }}">{{ t }}</span> {% endfor %}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ c.amcache_first_seen or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ c.userassist_run_count or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ c.userassist_last_run or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ c.shimcache_hits or "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if registry.corroborated_components %}
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Independent corroboration:</strong> {{ registry.corroborated_components }} file{{ "s" if registry.corroborated_components != 1 }} above {{ "is" if registry.corroborated_components == 1 else "are" }} confirmed by 2 or more separate OS subsystems (execution history, cache insertion, install record) agreeing independently — stronger than any single artifact type's say-so alone.
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No cross-referenceable registry components found.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Raw findings by hive</h2><span class="count">{{ registry.total_findings }} finding{{ "s" if registry.total_findings != 1 }}, deduplicated — what the table above was built from</span></div>
    {% if registry.sections %}
    <details class="appendix">
      <summary>Show per-hive detail</summary>
      <div class="appendix-body">
        {% for s in registry.sections %}
        <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;">
          <h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">{{ s.label }}</h3>
          <span class="count"><span class="chip {{ 'high' if s.confidence == 'high' else ('low' if s.confidence == 'low' else '') }}">{{ s.confidence }}</span> {{ s.findings|length }} finding{{ "s" if s.findings|length != 1 }}</span>
        </div>
        <div class="table-scroll">
          <table class="evidence-table">
            <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Detail</th><th>Timestamp</th><th>Occ.</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {% for f in s.findings %}
              <tr>
                <td class="val">{{ f.path or "—" }}</td>
                <td class="val">
                  {% if s.type == 'UserAssist' %}run_count={{ f.run_count }}, focus_count={{ f.focus_count }}, focus_time_ms={{ f.total_focus_time_ms }}
                  {% elif s.type == 'Amcache' %}sha1={{ f.sha1 or "—" }}, size={{ f.size or "—" }}
                  {% else %}{{ f.description }}
                  {% endif %}
                </td>
                <td class="off">{{ f.timestamp or "—" }}</td>
                <td class="off">{{ f.occurrences }}{% if f.occurrences > 1 %} (collapsed dup.){% endif %}</td>
              </tr>
              {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No Tor-related registry artifacts found in the provided hives.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk %}
  <div class="band">
    <div class="eyebrow">Module B</div>
    <h2>Disk — Tor Browser profile, Tor daemon &amp; downloaded files</h2>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
      <dt>Sources analyzed</dt><dd>{{ disk.supplied|join(", ") }}</dd>
      {% if disk.profile %}
      <dt>Profile integrity</dt>
      <dd>{% if disk.profile.integrity.manifest_status == 'verified' %}<span class="flag-ok">✓ {{ disk.profile.integrity.hashed_files }} files verified against acquisition manifest</span>{% else %}<span class="flag-warn">⚠ No acquisition manifest — {{ disk.profile.integrity.hashed_files }} files hashed at analysis time only</span>{% endif %}{% if disk.profile.integrity.source_unchanged %} · source unchanged after analysis{% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.daemon %}
      <dt>Daemon dir integrity</dt>
      <dd>{% if disk.daemon.integrity.manifest_status == 'verified' %}<span class="flag-ok">✓ {{ disk.daemon.integrity.hashed_files }} files verified against acquisition manifest</span>{% else %}<span class="flag-warn">⚠ No acquisition manifest — {{ disk.daemon.integrity.hashed_files }} files hashed at analysis time only</span>{% endif %}{% if disk.daemon.integrity.source_unchanged %} · source unchanged after analysis{% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.downloads %}
      <dt>Volume scanned</dt><dd>{{ disk.downloads.volume_root }} — {{ "{:,}".format(disk.downloads.files_walked) }} files walked in {{ disk.downloads.scan_seconds }}s</dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
  </div>

  {% if disk.errors %}
  <section>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Sections that failed:</strong> everything below comes from the sources that parsed cleanly.
      <ul style="margin:8px 0 0; padding-left:18px;">
        {% for name, err in disk.errors.items() %}
        <li class="mono" style="font-size:12px;">{{ name }}: {{ err }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Summary</h2></div>
    <div class="tiles">
      {% if disk.daemon %}
      <div class="tile{{ '' if disk.daemon.daemon_start else ' gap' }}">
        <h3>Tor daemon session</h3>
        {% if disk.daemon.daemon_start %}
        <p>Daemon running from <span class="mono">{{ disk.daemon.daemon_start }}</span> to at least <span class="mono">{{ disk.daemon.state_written or disk.daemon.daemon_start }}</span>. {{ disk.daemon.guards_used|length }} guard{{ "s" if disk.daemon.guards_used|length != 1 }} actually routed traffic; {{ disk.daemon.circuits_built or "?" }} circuits built over the daemon's life.</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>No <span class="mono">lock</span> file — daemon start time unknown.</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.downloads %}
      <div class="tile{{ '' if disk.downloads.inside else ' gap' }}">
        <h3>Internet-origin files</h3>
        <p>{{ disk.downloads.hits|length }} file{{ "s" if disk.downloads.hits|length != 1 }} on the whole volume carr{{ "ies" if disk.downloads.hits|length == 1 else "y" }} a <span class="mono">Zone.Identifier</span> stream{% if disk.downloads.window %}; {{ disk.downloads.inside }} created while the Tor daemon was running, {{ disk.downloads.outside }} outside that window{% else %}; no daemon window to correlate against{% endif %}.</p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.residue %}
      <div class="tile{{ '' if disk.residue.any_hits else ' gap' }}">
        <h3>Memory residue on disk</h3>
        {% if disk.residue.any_hits %}
        <p>{{ disk.residue.addresses|length }} onion address{{ "es" if disk.residue.addresses|length != 1 }} recovered from paged/hibernated memory — the only disk source that can name a public service.</p>
        {% for a in disk.residue.addresses %}<span class="tile-value">{{ a.address }}</span>{% endfor %}
        {% else %}
        <p>{{ disk.residue.files|length }} memory file{{ "s" if disk.residue.files|length != 1 }} carved, no onion address. Visited public services are not recoverable from this disk.</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.ntfs and disk.ntfs.addresses %}
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Filesystem metadata</h3>
        <p>{{ disk.ntfs.addresses|length }} onion address{{ "es" if disk.ntfs.addresses|length != 1 }} recorded by NTFS{% if disk.ntfs.addresses|selectattr("deleted")|list %}, {{ disk.ntfs.addresses|selectattr("deleted")|list|length }} for files since deleted{% endif %}{% if disk.ntfs.deleted_downloads %}; {{ disk.ntfs.deleted_downloads|length }} deleted download{{ "s" if disk.ntfs.deleted_downloads|length != 1 }} still marked internet-origin{% endif %}.</p>
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.profile %}
      <div class="tile{{ ' gap' if disk.profile.inert }}">
        <h3>Browser profile</h3>
        {% if disk.profile.inert %}
        <p>No history, cookies or bookmarks beyond Tor Browser's {{ disk.profile.default_entries }} shipped defaults. Expected: permanent private browsing never writes them. This is not evidence of no activity.</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>{{ disk.profile.history|length }} visited page{{ "s" if disk.profile.history|length != 1 }}, {{ disk.profile.cookies|length }} cookie{{ "s" if disk.profile.cookies|length != 1 }}, {{ disk.profile.bookmarks|length }} user bookmark{{ "s" if disk.profile.bookmarks|length != 1 }} — unusual for Tor Browser; check whether private browsing was disabled.</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.daemon and disk.daemon.credentials %}
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Configured hidden services</h3>
        <p>{{ disk.daemon.credentials|length }} client-auth credential{{ "s" if disk.daemon.credentials|length != 1 }} name{{ "s" if disk.daemon.credentials|length == 1 }} a specific onion service in plaintext.</p>
        {% for c in disk.daemon.credentials %}<span class="tile-value">{{ c.onion_address }}</span>{% endfor %}
      </div>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </section>

  {% if disk.daemon %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Tor daemon activity</h2><span class="count">from <span class="mono">Data/Tor</span> — persisted across restarts, outside private-browsing scope</span></div>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
      <dt>Tor version</dt><dd>{{ disk.daemon.tor_version or "—" }}</dd>
      <dt>Daemon started</dt><dd>{{ disk.daemon.daemon_start or "— (no lock file)" }}</dd>
      <dt>State last written</dt><dd>{{ disk.daemon.state_written or "—" }}{% if disk.daemon.guest_local_written %} <span style="color:var(--ink-muted)">(guest clock: {{ disk.daemon.guest_local_written }}{% if disk.daemon.guest_utc_offset_hours is not none %}, UTC{{ "%+g"|format(disk.daemon.guest_utc_offset_hours) }}h{% endif %})</span>{% endif %}</dd>
      {% if disk.daemon.minutes_since_user_activity is not none %}
      <dt>Idle at last write</dt><dd>{{ disk.daemon.minutes_since_user_activity }} min since user activity{% if disk.daemon.dormant %} · dormant={{ disk.daemon.dormant }}{% endif %}</dd>
      {% endif %}
      <dt>Circuits built</dt><dd>{{ disk.daemon.circuits_built or "—" }}{% if disk.daemon.histogram_consistent is false %} <span class="flag-warn">⚠ build-time histogram does not sum to this — state file truncated or edited</span>{% endif %}</dd>
      {% if disk.daemon.consensus %}
      <dt>Consensus</dt><dd>valid {{ disk.daemon.consensus.valid_after }} → {{ disk.daemon.consensus.valid_until }} <span style="color:var(--ink-muted)">(authority-signed; independent of the guest clock)</span></dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
    <div class="section-head"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Entry guards that carried traffic</h3><span class="count">{{ disk.daemon.guards_used|length }} of {{ disk.daemon.guards_sampled }} sampled</span></div>
    {% if disk.daemon.guards_used %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Nickname</th><th>RSA id</th><th>Confirmed</th><th>Uses ok/tried</th><th>Circuits ok/tried</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for g in disk.daemon.guards_used %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ g.nickname }}</td><td class="off">{{ g.rsa_id }}</td><td class="off">{{ g.confirmed_on or "—" }}</td><td class="mono">{{ g.use }}</td><td class="mono">{{ g.circuits }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No guard has a recorded use — the daemon may never have built a working circuit.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.daemon.credentials %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Client-auth credentials</h3><span class="count">configuration, not proof of a visit</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Onion address</th><th>File</th><th>Modified</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in disk.daemon.credentials %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ c.onion_address }}</td><td class="val">{{ c.filename }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.modified or "—" }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.sha256[:12] ~ "…" if c.sha256 else "—" }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if disk.daemon.ignored_auth_files %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px;">Ignored by tor (wrong extension): <span class="mono">{{ disk.daemon.ignored_auth_files|join(", ") }}</span></p>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk.downloads %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Internet-origin files</h2><span class="count">{{ disk.downloads.hits|length }} on the whole volume, no folder assumed</span></div>
    <div class="ribbon">
      <strong>Network origin and timing, not the source site.</strong> Windows tags every file a browser saves from the network with a <span class="mono">Zone.Identifier</span> stream; locally created or USB/ISO-copied files never carry one. Tor Browser deliberately omits the <span class="mono">HostUrl</span>/<span class="mono">ReferrerUrl</span> fields other browsers write there, so the originating address is not recoverable from the file. Only the last Tor session's window is reconstructable from daemon artifacts.
    </div>
    {% if disk.downloads.window %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:12px;">Tor daemon window used for correlation: <span class="mono">{{ disk.downloads.window.start }}</span> → <span class="mono">{{ disk.downloads.window.end }}</span>.</p>
    {% elif 'tor_daemon' in disk.supplied %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:12px;">No daemon window could be derived (missing <span class="mono">lock</span> or <span class="mono">state</span>) — files are listed without correlation.</p>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:12px;">Supply <span class="mono">--tor-dir</span> alongside <span class="mono">--disk-root</span> to correlate these against the Tor daemon's session window.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.downloads.hits %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Path on volume</th><th>Created (NTFS)</th><th>Tor running?</th><th>Zone</th><th>Size</th><th>SHA-256</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for h in disk.downloads.hits %}
          <tr>
            <td class="val">{{ h.path }}{% if h.host_url or h.referrer_url %}<br><span class="off">host={{ h.host_url or "—" }} referrer={{ h.referrer_url or "—" }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ h.created or h.modified or "—" }}{% if h.timestamp_source != 'ntfs' %}<br>(mtime; no NTFS times){% endif %}</td>
            <td>{% if h.within_window is true %}<span class="chip high">yes</span>{% elif h.within_window is false %}<span class="chip low">no</span>{% else %}<span class="chip">unknown</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ h.zone_id if h.zone_id is not none else "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ "{:,}".format(h.size) }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ h.sha256[:12] }}…</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if disk.downloads.xattr_support is false %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px;"><span class="flag-warn">⚠</span> Volume not mounted through ntfs-3g — NTFS creation times unavailable, modification times shown instead.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No file on the volume carries a <span class="mono">Zone.Identifier</span> stream.{% if disk.downloads.xattr_support is none %} If the volume was not mounted through ntfs-3g the stream is invisible to this scan, so this is not proof that nothing was downloaded.{% endif %}</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk.residue %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Memory residue on disk</h2><span class="count">pagefile, swapfile, hibernation file, crash dumps</span></div>
    <div class="ribbon">
      <strong>The one disk route to a public onion address.</strong> Tor Browser and the tor daemon keep visited addresses in memory only; these files are where Windows itself writes memory to disk. A hit proves the string was in RAM at some point — not when, and not which process held it.{% if disk.residue.hibernation_present %} <span class="mono">hiberfil.sys</span> is compressed: its counts are a lower bound, and a Volatility3 hibernation-layer pass would read it fully.{% endif %}
    </div>
    {% if disk.residue.files %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Kind</th><th>Size</th><th>Modified</th><th>Onion addrs</th><th>Credentials</th><th>Tor markers</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for f in disk.residue.files %}
          <tr>
            <td class="val">{{ f.path }}{% if f.compressed %}<br><span class="off">compressed — lower bound</span>{% endif %}{% if f.error %}<br><span class="chip error">error</span> <span class="off">{{ f.error }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ f.kind.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ "{:,}".format(f.size) }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ f.modified or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ f.onion_count }}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ f.credential_count }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ f.markers|join(", ") if f.markers else "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if disk.residue.addresses %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Onion addresses recovered from memory residue</h3><span class="count">{{ disk.residue.addresses|length }}</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Address</th><th>Occurrences</th><th>In</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for a in disk.residue.addresses %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ a.address }}</td><td class="mono">{{ a.occurrences }}</td><td class="val">{{ a.files|join(", ") }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:12px;">No onion address in any of these files. With enough RAM and no hibernation, Windows may never have paged Tor Browser out — a modified time older than the Tor session (see above) means the pagefile was not even written during it.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No pagefile, swapfile, hibernation file or crash dump on this volume.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk.ntfs or disk.notes.ntfs %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>NTFS metadata</h2><span class="count">$MFT records and the $UsnJrnl change journal</span></div>
    {% if disk.notes.ntfs %}
    <p class="note"><span class="flag-warn">⚠</span> Not analyzed — {{ disk.notes.ntfs }}.</p>
    {% else %}
    <div class="ribbon">
      <strong>Written by the filesystem, not by Tor Browser.</strong> The MFT keeps names, timestamps and small contents of deleted files until their record is reused; the change journal logs every create, write, rename and delete by name. Both outlive the files, so a client-auth credential the user later removed, or a download later deleted, can still be named here.
    </div>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:18px;">
      <dt>$MFT</dt><dd>{% if disk.ntfs.mft_available %}{{ "{:,}".format(disk.ntfs.mft_records) }} named records{% else %}— not available{% endif %}</dd>
      <dt>$UsnJrnl</dt><dd>{% if disk.ntfs.usn_available %}{{ "{:,}".format(disk.ntfs.usn_records) }} records, {{ disk.ntfs.journal_first or "?" }} → {{ disk.ntfs.journal_last or "?" }}{% else %}— not available{% endif %}</dd>
      {% if disk.ntfs.window %}
      <dt>Tor file activity</dt><dd>{{ disk.ntfs.window.events }} journal events on Tor Browser/daemon files, {{ disk.ntfs.window.first }} → {{ disk.ntfs.window.last }}</dd>
      {% endif %}
    </dl>
    {% if disk.ntfs.addresses %}
    <div class="section-head"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Onion addresses in filesystem metadata</h3><span class="count">{{ disk.ntfs.addresses|length }}</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Address</th><th>Recorded in</th><th>Where</th><th>File status</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for a in disk.ntfs.addresses %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ a.address }}</td><td class="mono">{{ a.sources|join(", ") }}</td><td class="val">{{ a.paths|join("; ") }}</td><td>{% if a.deleted %}<span class="chip low">deleted</span>{% elif a.filename_evidence %}<span class="chip ok">present</span>{% else %}<span class="chip">file content</span>{% endif %}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if disk.ntfs.resident_onion_files %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px;">Addresses found inside small files stored in the MFT itself: {% for r in disk.ntfs.resident_onion_files %}<span class="mono">{{ r.path }}</span>{{ " (deleted)" if r.deleted }}{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %} — check whether these are the examiner's own transfer files before counting them as browsing evidence.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No onion address appears in any filename, journal entry or MFT-resident file content.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.ntfs.downloads %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Downloads reconstructed from the change journal</h3><span class="count">{{ disk.ntfs.downloads|length }} — temp-file naming identifies the browser family</span></div>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Browser attribution.</strong> Firefox — and therefore Tor Browser — saves a download as <span class="mono">&lt;8 random chars&gt;.&lt;ext&gt;.part</span>, then renames it to the final name and stamps <span class="mono">Zone.Identifier</span>; Chromium uses <span class="mono">.crdownload</span>, legacy Edge/IE <span class="mono">.partial</span>. The journal records that sequence by name, so it survives the file being deleted and it names the family that wrote it. Attribution to Tor Browser specifically holds when it is the only Firefox-family browser on the machine.
    </div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Started</th><th>Completed</th><th>Browser family</th><th>Tor running?</th><th>Zone stamped</th><th>Deleted</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for d in disk.ntfs.downloads %}
          <tr>
            <td class="val">{{ d.path }}<br><span class="off">via {{ d.temp_name }}</span></td>
            <td class="off">{{ d.started or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ d.completed or "—" }}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ d.browser_family.replace('_', ' ') }}</td>
            <td>{% if d.within_window is true %}<span class="chip high">yes</span>{% elif d.within_window is false %}<span class="chip low">no</span>{% else %}<span class="chip">unknown</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ "yes" if d.zone_stamped else "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ d.deleted or "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.ntfs.deleted_downloads %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Deleted internet-origin files</h3><span class="count">Zone.Identifier survives in the MFT record</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Path</th><th>Created</th><th>Zone</th><th>MFT record</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for d in disk.ntfs.deleted_downloads %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ d.path }}</td><td class="off">{{ d.created or "—" }}</td><td class="mono">{{ d.zone_id if d.zone_id is not none else "—" }}</td><td class="mono">{{ d.record }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.ntfs.events %}
    <details class="appendix" style="margin-top:22px;">
      <summary>Show {{ disk.ntfs.events|length }} journal event{{ "s" if disk.ntfs.events|length != 1 }} on Tor Browser / daemon files{% if disk.ntfs.deleted_tor_files %} and {{ disk.ntfs.deleted_tor_files|length }} deleted Tor-related file{{ "s" if disk.ntfs.deleted_tor_files|length != 1 }}{% endif %}</summary>
      <div class="appendix-body">
        {% if disk.ntfs.deleted_tor_files %}
        <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:10px;">Deleted (MFT record not in use, name retained):</p>
        {% for d in disk.ntfs.deleted_tor_files[:200] %}
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">{{ d.path }}</span><span class="why">{{ d.modified or "—" }}</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
        {% endif %}
        <p class="note" style="margin:14px 0 10px;">Change journal, oldest first{% if disk.ntfs.events|length > 500 %} (first 500 shown){% endif %}:</p>
        {% for e in disk.ntfs.events[:500] %}
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">{{ e.time or "—" }} · {{ e.path }}</span><span class="why">{{ e.reasons }}</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {% endif %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk.profile %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Browser profile</h2><span class="count">{{ disk.profile.places_rows }} places rows, {{ disk.profile.default_entries }} shipped defaults, {{ disk.profile.history_visits }} recorded visits</span></div>
    {% if disk.profile.errors %}
    <div class="callout"><strong>Unreadable:</strong> {% for name, err in disk.profile.errors.items() %}<span class="mono">{{ name }}</span> — {{ err }}{{ "; " if not loop.last }}{% endfor %}. Absence below is not established for these files.</div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.inert %}
    <div class="callout"><strong>Expected inert profile.</strong> Tor Browser runs in permanent private browsing: <span class="mono">places.sqlite</span> keeps only the shipped Tor Project bookmarks and never records visits, downloads or cookies. An empty table here is the normal state after real use — the daemon and volume sections above carry the activity evidence.</div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.history %}
    <div class="section-head"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Visited pages</h3><span class="count">excluding shipped defaults</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>URL</th><th>Title</th><th>Visits</th><th>Typed</th><th>Last visit</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for h in disk.profile.history %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ h.url }}</td><td class="val">{{ h.title or "—" }}</td><td class="mono">{{ h.visit_count }}</td><td class="mono">{{ "yes" if h.typed else "—" }}</td><td class="off">{{ h.last_visit or "—" }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.download_records %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Download records</h3><span class="count">from places.sqlite annotations</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Source URL</th><th>Saved to</th><th>Added</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for d in disk.profile.download_records %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ d.source_url }}</td><td class="val">{{ d.destination }}</td><td class="off">{{ d.added or "—" }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.cookies %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">Cookies</h3><span class="count">{{ disk.profile.cookies|length }}</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Host</th><th>Name</th><th>Created</th><th>Last accessed</th><th>Expires</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in disk.profile.cookies %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ c.host }}</td><td class="val">{{ c.name }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.created or "—" }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.last_accessed or "—" }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.expires or "—" }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.bookmarks %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;"><h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">User bookmarks</h3><span class="count">from bookmark backups, excluding shipped defaults</span></div>
    <div class="path-list">
      {% for b in disk.profile.bookmarks %}<span class="path-pill">{{ b.uri }}{% if b.title %} <span style="color:var(--ink-muted)">— {{ b.title }}</span>{% endif %}</span>{% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.profile.favicon_pages %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:14px;">Favicon cache also references: <span class="mono">{{ disk.profile.favicon_pages|join(", ") }}</span></p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% if disk.carve %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Raw image carve</h2><span class="count">byte-level scan incl. unallocated space</span></div>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:14px;">
      <dt>Image</dt><dd>{{ disk.carve.image }}</dd>
      <dt>SHA-256</dt><dd>{{ disk.carve.image_sha256 }}</dd>
    </dl>
    {% if disk.carve.addresses %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Onion address</th><th>Occurrences</th><th>First offsets</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for a in disk.carve.addresses %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ a.address }}</td><td class="mono">{{ a.occurrences }}</td><td class="off">{{ a.first_offsets|join(", ") }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No onion addresses carved from the image.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if disk.carve.credentials %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:8px;">Client-auth credential bytes found for: <span class="mono">{{ disk.carve.credentials|join(", ") }}</span> — presence alone does not prove a visit.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endif %}
  {% endif %}

  {% if memory %}
  {% set d = memory.details %}
  <div class="band">
    <div class="eyebrow">Module C</div>
    <h2>Memory — Tor Browser process dump</h2>
    <dl class="meta-grid" style="margin-bottom:32px;">
      <dt>Dump file</dt><dd>{{ d.dump.path.split('/')[-1].split('\\')[-1] }}</dd>
      <dt>Size</dt><dd>{{ "{:,}".format(d.dump.size_bytes) }} bytes ({{ "%.1f"|format(d.dump.size_bytes / 1048576) }} MiB)</dd>
      <dt>SHA-256</dt><dd>{{ d.dump.sha256 }}</dd>
      <dt>Integrity</dt>
      <dd>
        {% if d.dump.integrity_verified == true %}<span class="flag-ok">✓ Verified against .sha256 sidecar</span>
        {% else %}<span class="flag-warn">⚠ Unverified — no .sha256 sidecar alongside this copy</span>
        {% endif %}
      </dd>
      <dt>Target onion</dt><dd>{{ d.targeting.onion or "— not supplied" }}</dd>
      <dt>Target host</dt><dd>{{ d.targeting.host or "— not supplied" }}</dd>
      <dt>Username</dt><dd>{{ d.targeting.username or "— not supplied this run" }}</dd>
    </dl>
  </div>

  {% if d.targeting_suggestions %}
  <section>
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Heads up:</strong> onion address(es) seen repeatedly in memory but not covered by <span class="mono">--onion</span>/<span class="mono">--host</span> (Tor Browser's own bundled default services also land here — check before assuming a missed target):
      <ul style="margin:8px 0 0; padding-left:18px;">
        {% for s in d.targeting_suggestions %}
        <li class="mono" style="font-size:12px;">{{ s.onion }} (seen {{ s.hit_count }}×)</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Summary</h2></div>
    <div class="tiles">
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Session &amp; cookie evidence</h3>
        <p>{{ memory.session_cookies|length }} high-confidence value{{ "s" if memory.session_cookies|length != 1 }} recovered from the cookie jar.</p>
        {% for c in memory.session_cookies %}{% if c.decoded_payload %}<span class="tile-value">{{ c.decoded_payload }}</span>{% endif %}{% endfor %}
      </div>
      <div class="tile">
        <h3>Site map</h3>
        <p>{{ memory.site_map|length }} distinct path{{ "s" if memory.site_map|length != 1 }} recovered on the target.
        {% if memory.near_duplicates %}{{ memory.near_duplicates|length }} look like possible typos/probes.{% endif %}</p>
      </div>
      <div class="tile{{ '' if memory.downloads.matched else ' gap' }}">
        <h3>Local downloads</h3>
        {% if memory.downloads.matched %}
        <p>{{ memory.downloads.matched|length }} file{{ "s" if memory.downloads.matched|length != 1 }} confirmed under a real <span class="mono">Downloads</span> folder, matched to a target-site path.</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>No downloads correlate to a target-site path in this dump.</p>
        {% endif %}
        {% if memory.downloads.unmatched %}
        <p class="note">+ {{ memory.downloads.unmatched|length }} other download{{ "s" if memory.downloads.unmatched|length != 1 }} seen on this machine, not correlated to the target site — see below.</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="tile{{ '' if d.key_findings.credentials else ' gap' }}">
        <h3>Credentials</h3>
        {% if d.key_findings.credentials %}
        <p>{{ d.key_findings.credentials|length }} high-confidence submission{{ "s" if d.key_findings.credentials|length != 1 }} recovered.</p>
        {% else %}
        <p>No plaintext <span class="mono">field=value</span> or JSON-shaped login submission found in memory. Not proof no login happened — session cookie evidence already establishes that independently; this data type just wasn't in a text-matchable shape (or was overwritten) by capture time.</p>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Session &amp; cookies</h2><span class="count">{{ memory.session_cookies|length }} unique, high-confidence</span></div>
    {% if memory.session_cookies %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Value</th><th>First offset</th><th>Occ.</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in memory.session_cookies %}
          <tr>
            <td class="val">{{ c.name }}</td>
            <td class="val">{{ c.value }}{% if c.decoded_payload %}<br><span style="color:var(--ink-muted)">↳ decodes to {{ c.decoded_payload }}</span>{% endif %}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ c.offset }}</td>
            <td class="mono">{{ c.occurrences }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No high-confidence session/cookie values recovered.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  {% if d.key_findings.credentials %}
  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Credentials</h2><span class="count">{{ d.key_findings.credentials|length }} unique, high-confidence</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th><th>Shape</th><th>First offset</th><th>Occ.</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for c in d.key_findings.credentials %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ c.field }}</td><td class="val">{{ c.value }}</td><td class="mono">{{ c.shape }}</td><td class="off">{{ c.offset }}</td><td class="mono">{{ c.occurrences }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Site map</h2><span class="count">{{ memory.site_map|length }} distinct paths</span></div>
    <div class="path-list">
      {% for p in memory.site_map %}
      <span class="path-pill{{ ' odd' if p in memory.near_duplicates }}">{{ p }}</span>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
    {% if memory.near_duplicates %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:10px;">
      {% for p, close in memory.near_duplicates.items() %}
      <strong style="color:var(--noise)">{{ p }}</strong> closely resembles {{ close|join(", ") }} — possible typo, stray keystroke, or manual endpoint probing.<br>
      {% endfor %}
    </p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if memory.assets %}
    <p class="note" style="margin-top:10px;">+ {{ memory.assets|length }} automatic asset request{{ "s" if memory.assets|length != 1 }} (<span class="mono">{{ memory.assets|join(", ") }}</span>) — page-load traffic, not user actions; kept out of the sequence below.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Local downloads</h2><span class="count">{{ memory.downloads.matched|length }} matched to a target-site path</span></div>
    {% if memory.downloads.matched %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>File</th><th>Matches site endpoint</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for dl in memory.downloads.matched %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ dl.value }}</td><td class="val">{{ dl.matched_endpoint }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No downloads correlate to a target-site path.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% if memory.downloads.unmatched %}
    <details class="appendix" style="margin-top:14px;">
      <summary>Show {{ memory.downloads.unmatched|length }} other download{{ "s" if memory.downloads.unmatched|length != 1 }} seen on this machine — not correlated to the target site</summary>
      <div class="appendix-body">
        <p class="note" style="margin-bottom:10px;">This is a full-memory image: a <span class="mono">Users\*\Downloads\</span> path anywhere on the machine — any user account, any application, unrelated installers — shows up here, not just this investigation's target. None of these correlate to a recovered target-site path; treat them as machine-wide context, not evidence tied to the target.</p>
        {% for dl in memory.downloads.unmatched %}
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">{{ dl.value }}</span></div>
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </details>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Search / typed terms</h2><span class="count">by occurrence count</span></div>
    {% if memory.search_terms %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Term</th><th>Occurrences</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for t in memory.search_terms %}
          <tr><td class="val">{{ t.value }}{% if t.matches_username %}<span class="chip high" style="margin-left:6px;">matches --username</span>{% endif %}</td><td class="mono">{{ t.count }}</td></tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No non-template search terms recovered.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Reconstructed activity sequence</h2><span class="count">{{ memory.events|length }} events, offset-ordered</span></div>
    <div class="ribbon"><strong>Not a verified timeline.</strong> {{ d.timeline.disclaimer }}</div>
    {% if memory.events %}
    <ol class="sequence">
      {% for e in memory.events %}
      <li>
        <div><span class="seq-type">{{ e.type }}</span>{{ e.detail }}{% if e.clustered_with_prev %}<span class="seq-flag">‡ clustered</span>{% endif %}{% if e.far_from_start %}<span class="seq-flag">† storage-region caveat</span>{% endif %}</div>
        <div class="seq-off">{{ e.offset }}</div>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ol>
    {% if memory.any_clustered %}
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>‡ Clustered events:</strong> events flagged with ‡ sit within {{ "{:,}".format(memory.cluster_gap_bytes) }} bytes of the previous one — tight enough to more likely be one rendered page's set of links (e.g. a dashboard listing everything at once) than separate sequential navigations. Treat clustered runs as "seen together," not necessarily "done in that exact order."
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% if memory.any_far_from_start %}
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>† Storage-region caveat:</strong> events flagged with † sit far past the sequence's typical spacing from the earliest event. Cookie/session and download-manager data live in their own memory regions, separate from rendered page content — a late offset here reflects where that data happens to sit in memory, not when it was created. Don't read these as "happened last."
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">No timeline events recovered.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head">
      <h2>Process &amp; system context (Volatility3)</h2>
      <span class="count">independent structural pass — never merged with string-carver evidence above</span>
    </div>
    <div class="ribbon">
      <strong>A second, independent method, not a second string carver.</strong> Everything below comes from
      parsing kernel data structures (process pool allocations, network/file/registry state), not from
      scanning bytes for text patterns — see each row's <span class="mono">source</span> tag. It can confirm
      <em>which process</em> and <em>when</em> in ways raw string carving can't, but needs kernel symbols
      matching the imaged OS build to run at all.
    </div>
    {% if memory.volatility3.status == 'skipped' %}
    <p class="note">Not run this pass — {{ memory.volatility3.message }}.</p>
    {% elif memory.volatility3.status == 'error' %}
    <p class="note"><span class="chip error">error</span> Volatility3 could not be invoked at all — {{ memory.volatility3.message }}</p>
    {% else %}
    {% if memory.volatility3.corroboration %}
    <div class="callout">
      <strong>Independent corroboration:</strong> the notes below point out where this structural pass and the
      string-carver evidence above happen to agree — a human-readable juxtaposition, not an automated score.
      <ul style="margin:8px 0 0; padding-left:18px;">
        {% for note in memory.volatility3.corroboration %}
        <li>{{ note }}</li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </div>
    {% endif %}
    {% for p in memory.volatility3.plugins %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:22px;">
      <h3 style="font-size:15px; font-weight:600;">{{ p.label }}</h3>
      <span class="count mono">source: volatility3:{{ p.name }}</span>
    </div>
    {% if p.status == 'ok' %}
    {% if p.rows %}
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead>
          <tr>
            {% for col in p.rows[0].keys() if col != 'source' %}
            <th>{{ col }}</th>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for row in p.rows %}
          <tr>
            {% for col, val in row.items() if col != 'source' %}
            <td class="val">{{ val if val is not none else "—" }}</td>
            {% endfor %}
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% if p.truncated %}
    <p class="note">Showing {{ p.rows|length }} of {{ p.total_rows }} rows.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note">Ran cleanly, no rows returned.</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% else %}
    <p class="note"><span class="chip error">error</span> {{ p.message }}</p>
    {% endif %}
    {% endfor %}
    {% endif %}
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="section-head"><h2>Filtered as noise</h2><span class="count">kept for transparency, not evidentiary</span></div>
    <details class="appendix">
      <summary>Show unfiltered context — {{ "{:,}".format(d.unfiltered.total_strings_extracted) }} printable strings scanned in total</summary>
      <div class="appendix-body">
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">Cookie/credential regex hits, low-confidence</span><span class="why">{{ d.targeted.cookies|selectattr("confidence","equalto","low")|list|length }} cookie + {{ d.targeted.credentials|selectattr("confidence","equalto","low")|list|length }} credential hits look like Firefox's own printf format strings, not real values</span></div>
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">Download-path regex hits, low-confidence</span><span class="why">{{ d.targeted.downloads|selectattr("confidence","equalto","low")|list|length }} paths outside a real Downloads folder — Tor Browser's own install/extension files</span></div>
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">Onion domains seen but not targeted</span><span class="why">{{ d.targeting_suggestions|length }} — see the callout above if any</span></div>
        <div class="appendix-row"><span class="val">Unanchored URL-like strings</span><span class="why">{{ d.unfiltered.urls.count }} total seen, not evidence on their own — includes Firefox's own code/strings</span></div>
      </div>
    </details>
  </section>
  {% endif %}

  {% for g in generic_modules %}
  <div class="band">
    <div class="eyebrow">{{ g.name }}</div>
    <h2>{{ g.name.replace('module_', '').replace('_', ' — ', 1)|title }}</h2>
  </div>
  <section>
    <p><span class="chip {{ g.status }}">{{ g.status.replace('_', ' ') }}</span>{% if g.message %} <span class="note">{{ g.message }}</span>{% endif %}</p>
    {% if g.artifacts %}
    <div class="section-head" style="margin-top:14px;"><h2 style="font-size:16px;">Artifacts</h2><span class="count">showing {{ g.artifacts|length }} of {{ g.total }}</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="evidence-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>Source</th><th>Description</th><th>SHA-256</th><th>Timestamp</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          {% for a in g.artifacts %}
          <tr>
            <td class="mono">{{ a.artifact_type }}</td>
            <td class="val">{{ a.source }}</td>
            <td class="val">{{ a.description }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ a.sha256[:12] ~ "…" if a.sha256 else "—" }}</td>
            <td class="off">{{ a.timestamp or "—" }}</td>
          </tr>
          {% endfor %}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {% elif g.status == 'ok' %}
    <p class="note">Ran cleanly, no artifacts reported.</p>
    {% elif g.status == 'not_implemented' %}
    <p class="note">This module has no implementation yet — nothing from this evidence layer contributes to the case until it does.</p>
    {% elif g.status == 'skipped' %}
    <p class="note">No evidence was supplied for this module this run.</p>
    {% endif %}
  </section>
  {% endfor %}

  <div class="band">
    <div class="eyebrow">Next steps</div>
    <h2>Recommendations</h2>
  </div>
  <section>
    <ul class="reco-list">
      {% if memory %}
      {% if not memory.details.targeting.username %}
      <li>Re-run with <span class="mono">--username &lt;candidate&gt;</span> to confirm which search term was the real login via the <span class="mono">matches_username</span> flag.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if memory.details.targeting_suggestions %}
      <li>Check the onion address(es) flagged in the memory section — re-run with <span class="mono">--onion</span> set to any that turn out to be a real missed target.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if not memory.details.key_findings.credentials %}
      <li>No plaintext credentials recovered from memory strings alone — for firmer proof of the login itself, correlate with server-side access logs or a disk-based artifact (browser saved-logins store, if enabled).</li>
      {% endif %}
      <li>If the source machine is still available, pull real filesystem MACB timestamps on the confirmed downloads — actual time data this memory-only view can't provide.</li>
      <li>Treat every ‡/† flag in the activity sequence as an investigative lead worth checking against another source, not as settled fact.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk %}
      {% if disk.downloads and disk.downloads.hits and not disk.downloads.window %}
      <li>Re-run with <span class="mono">--tor-dir</span> so the {{ disk.downloads.hits|length }} internet-origin file{{ "s" if disk.downloads.hits|length != 1 }} can be placed inside or outside the Tor daemon's session window.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.downloads and disk.downloads.inside %}
      <li>{{ disk.downloads.inside }} internet-origin file{{ "s were" if disk.downloads.inside != 1 else " was" }} created while Tor was running. The file itself cannot name its source; confirm the originating site from memory (Module C download/site-map correlation) or server-side logs.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.profile and disk.profile.inert and not disk.downloads %}
      <li>The profile is inert by design. Run with <span class="mono">--disk-root</span> on the mounted volume to find downloaded files anywhere on disk, and rely on the daemon section for session timing.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.residue and not disk.residue.any_hits and not disk.residue.hibernation_present %}
      <li>No memory residue reached disk. A visited public onion service can only come from memory: acquire RAM live (Module C), or, for the post-hibernation scenario, hibernate the machine before imaging so <span class="mono">hiberfil.sys</span> captures it.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if disk.notes.ntfs %}
      <li>Remount the volume with <span class="mono">-o ro,show_sys_files,streams_interface=windows</span> so <span class="mono">$MFT</span> and <span class="mono">$UsnJrnl</span> can be parsed for deleted credential files, deleted downloads and a file-level activity timeline.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% if not disk.daemon %}
      <li>Supply <span class="mono">--tor-dir</span> (<span class="mono">TorBrowser/Data/Tor</span>): the daemon directory is the one disk source that persists guard usage and session timing outside private-browsing scope.</li>
      {% endif %}
      {% endif %}
      {% for g in generic_modules if g.status != 'ok' %}
      <li><span class="mono">{{ g.name }}</span> did not contribute ({{ g.status.replace('_', ' ') }}){% if g.message %}: {{ g.message }}{% endif %}. Cross-layer correlation is incomplete until it does.</li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </section>

  <footer>
    <span>TRANCE · findings.json schema v{{ findings.schema_version }}</span>
    <span>{{ findings.generated_at }}</span>
  </footer>

</div>
</body>
</html>
